Fedora-only fix-up, kept here on purpose (the patch series must also apply to vanilla stable): kernel-ark's
kernel-7.2.10-0 carries a newer skl_int3472_handle_gpio_resources() than vanilla v7.2.10, which logs each
error with dev_err_probe() where it happens and has no err_msg variable. The fix "Set error state for SP9
GPIO types" sets err_msg on the Surface Pro 9 regulator failure path, as vanilla needs, so on kernel-ark
discrete.c fails to compile ("'err_msg' undeclared"). This logs the error with dev_err_probe() there
instead, as the neighbouring cases do on kernel-ark; the error is still returned. Drop this when
kernel-ark's discrete.c has err_msg again, or when linux-surface's patch stops using it.
---
diff --git a/patches/7.2/0013-cameras.patch b/patches/7.2/0013-cameras.patch
index 1f5d4be..f8fc961 100644
--- a/patches/7.2/0013-cameras.patch
+++ b/patches/7.2/0013-cameras.patch
@@ -1106,7 +1106,7 @@ index b2a54733d..6d65adb0a 100644
  		    dev_info(int3472->dev, "  register_regulator returned: %d\n", ret);
  		    if (ret) {
 -			dev_err(int3472->dev, "Failed to register type 0x02x: %d\n", type, ret);
-+			err_msg = "Failed to register regulator\n";
++			dev_err_probe(int3472->dev, ret, "Failed to register regulator\n");
  		    }
  		    break;
  		case 0x11:
